%% state_02b_task_review_workflow.mmd - TaskReviewWorkflow Status
%% Updated 2026-07-19.
%% Ref: app/modules/reviews/domain/task_review_workflow.ts
%% Ref: app/modules/reviews/actions/commands/*task_review*_command.ts
%% Note: workflow status is separate from task delivery status.

stateDiagram-v2
    [*] --> awaiting_review : Delivery-done task\nvisible on review board

    awaiting_review --> in_review : First required reviewer submits\nquorum not met
    awaiting_review --> awaiting_response : Required review quorum met

    in_review --> awaiting_response : Remaining required reviewer submits

    awaiting_response --> done : Reviewee accepts\ncompleted_review_count >= required_review_count
    awaiting_response --> disputed : Reviewee response/debate

    disputed --> reported : Reviewer or reviewee reports dispute
    disputed --> done : Resolved/accepted outside admin path

    reported --> ai_reviewing : System admin starts\nAI advisory evaluation
    ai_reviewing --> reported : AI callback returns\nadvisory result
    reported --> resolved : System admin resolves
    ai_reviewing --> resolved : System admin resolves\nduring AI review
    resolved --> done : Resolution applied\nor re-review completed
    reported --> done : Legacy/manual closure
    done --> [*]

    note right of awaiting_review
        Board projection, not delivery status.
        Normal task board can still show task as done.
    end note

    note right of in_review
        Required reviewers are selected by application code.
        Reviewee cannot review own task.
        Workflow fails if fewer than two eligible reviewers exist.
    end note

    note right of reported
        Workflow tables are storage/index layer.
        FK/check/quorum/report rules are application-owned.
        Admin queue reads reported/ai_reviewing/resolved.
    end note
